    <!-- ════════════════════════════ CHAPTER 1 — GIT ════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="git">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon green">🌿</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 1</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Git — Gitea</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card green">
          <div class="tool-logo">🌿</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Gitea</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Self-hosted Git Service</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">A lightweight, self-hosted Git service written in Go. Provides repositories, pull requests, issues, webhooks, and a REST API — all running on-prem with minimal resources.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card blue">
          <div class="tool-logo">🔗</div>
          <div class="tool-name">GiteaService</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Rails Integration Class</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">A Faraday-based service class in <code>app/services/gitea_service.rb</code> that wraps every Gitea API call — branch creation, PR data, diff fetching, webhook management.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What Gitea Does</h2>
      <p>Gitea acts as the central source control server for all projects. It stores code repositories, accepts pushes from developers, fires webhook events to the Rails app (push, pull_request, release), and exposes a full REST API for programmatic access.</p>

      <h2>How It Connects to Rails</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="step-title">Webhook Registration</div>
            <div class="step-desc">When a project is linked to a Gitea repo, the app calls <code>GiteaService#create_webhook</code> to register a webhook pointing at <code>/webhooks/gitea</code>.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="step-title">Incoming Webhooks</div>
            <div class="step-desc"><code>WebhooksController#gitea</code> receives push/PR events, verifies the HMAC-SHA256 signature, and updates tickets, branches, and pull requests accordingly.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="step-title">Outgoing API calls</div>
            <div class="step-desc"><code>CreateBranchJob</code> and <code>SyncPullRequestJob</code> call <code>GiteaService</code> to create branches and pull full PR diff/file/comment data.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Configuration</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash (.env)</span><code><span class="c"># .env / credentials / ENV</span>
<span class="v">GITEA_URL</span>=<span class="s">http://gitea.local:3001</span>
<span class="v">GITEA_TOKEN</span>=<span class="s">ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</span>  <span class="c"># user access token</span>
<span class="v">GITEA_WEBHOOK_SECRET</span>=<span class="s">a_random_secret_string</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>GiteaService — Full Implementation</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="k">class</span> <span class="m">GiteaService</span>
  <span class="m">BASE_URL</span>  = <span class="m">ENV</span>.fetch(<span class="s">"GITEA_URL"</span>,   <span class="s">"http://localhost:3001"</span>)
  <span class="m">API_TOKEN</span> = <span class="m">ENV</span>.fetch(<span class="s">"GITEA_TOKEN"</span>, <span class="s">""</span>)

  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">initialize</span>
    @conn = <span class="m">Faraday</span>.new(url: <span class="m">BASE_URL</span>) <span class="k">do</span> |f|
      f.request  :json
      f.response :json
      f.headers[<span class="s">"Authorization"</span>] = <span class="s">"token #{API_TOKEN}"</span>
    <span class="k">end</span>
  <span class="k">end</span>

  <span class="c"># Create a branch for a ticket</span>
  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">create_branch</span>(repo_owner:, repo_name:, branch_name:, base_branch: <span class="s">"main"</span>)
    @conn.post(<span class="s">"/api/v1/repos/#{repo_owner}/#{repo_name}/branches"</span>) <span class="k">do</span> |req|
      req.body = { new_branch_name: branch_name, old_branch_name: base_branch }
    <span class="k">end</span>.then { |r| r.success? ? r.body : <span class="k">nil</span> }
  <span class="k">end</span>

  <span class="c"># Fetch PR diff (unified format)</span>
  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">pull_request_diff</span>(repo_owner:, repo_name:, pr_number:)
    <span class="m">Faraday</span>.get(
      <span class="s">"#{BASE_URL}/api/v1/repos/#{repo_owner}/#{repo_name}/pulls/#{pr_number}.diff"</span>,
      {}, { <span class="s">"Authorization"</span> => <span class="s">"token #{API_TOKEN}"</span>, <span class="s">"Accept"</span> => <span class="s">"text/plain"</span> }
    ).then { |r| r.success? ? r.body : <span class="k">nil</span> }
  <span class="k">end</span>

  <span class="c"># Verify HMAC-SHA256 webhook signature</span>
  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">self</span>.valid_signature?(payload, signature, secret)
    expected = <span class="s">"sha256=#{OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest(''sha256'', secret, payload)}"</span>
    <span class="m">ActiveSupport</span>::<span class="m">SecurityUtils</span>.secure_compare(expected, signature)
  <span class="k">end</span>
<span class="k">end</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>Webhook Handler</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="c"># app/controllers/webhooks_controller.rb</span>
<span class="k">class</span> <span class="m">WebhooksController</span> &lt; <span class="m">ActionController</span>::<span class="m">API</span>
  skip_before_action :verify_authenticity_token

  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">gitea</span>
    secret = <span class="m">ENV</span>[<span class="s">"GITEA_WEBHOOK_SECRET"</span>]
    sig    = request.headers[<span class="s">"X-Gitea-Signature"</span>]
    <span class="k">unless</span> <span class="m">GiteaService</span>.valid_signature?(request.raw_post, sig, secret)
      <span class="k">return</span> head :unauthorized
    <span class="k">end</span>

    event   = request.headers[<span class="s">"X-Gitea-Event"</span>]
    payload = <span class="m">JSON</span>.parse(request.raw_post)

    <span class="k">case</span> event
    <span class="k">when</span> <span class="s">"push"</span>         <span class="k">then</span> handle_push(payload)
    <span class="k">when</span> <span class="s">"pull_request"</span> <span class="k">then</span> handle_pull_request(payload)
    <span class="k">end</span>
    head :ok
  <span class="k">end</span>
<span class="k">end</span>
</code></pre>

      <div class="callout info">
        <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
        <p><strong>Install:</strong> Download the Gitea binary from <a href="https://gitea.io/en-us/download" target="_blank">gitea.io</a>, or run via Docker: <code>docker run -p 3001:3000 -v gitea:/data gitea/gitea:latest</code></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ════════════════════════════ CHAPTER 2 — CI ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="ci">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon orange">🔧</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 2</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">CI — Jenkins</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>Jenkins is the Continuous Integration server. It watches Gitea via webhook, runs builds and test suites on every commit, then POSTs results back to DevTeam Hub so developers can see CI status alongside their tickets and PRs.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card orange">
          <div class="tool-logo">🔧</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Jenkins</div>
          <div class="tool-type">CI/CD Automation Server</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Open-source automation server. Runs pipelines defined as <code>Jenkinsfile</code>, supports parallel stages, test reporting, artifact archiving, and hundreds of plugins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card blue">
          <div class="tool-logo">📡</div>
          <div class="tool-name">JenkinsService</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Rails Integration Class</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Calls the Jenkins REST API to trigger builds, fetch logs, and retrieve test results. Used by <code>CiRun</code> model updates and the CI dashboard.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>CI Pipeline Flow</h2>
      <div class="arch-diagram">
