      <h2>Jenkinsfile (Rails Project)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">groovy</span><code><span class="c">// Jenkinsfile — place in repo root</span>
pipeline {
  agent any
  environment {
    <span class="v">RAILS_ENV</span> = <span class="s">''test''</span>
    <span class="v">DEVTEAM_URL</span> = credentials(<span class="s">''devteam-api-url''</span>)
    <span class="v">DEVTEAM_TOKEN</span> = credentials(<span class="s">''devteam-api-token''</span>)
  }
  stages {
    stage(<span class="s">''Setup''</span>) {
      steps {
        sh <span class="s">''bundle install --jobs 4''</span>
        sh <span class="s">''bin/rails db:create db:migrate''</span>
      }
    }
    stage(<span class="s">''Tests''</span>) {
      steps {
        sh <span class="s">''bundle exec rspec --format RspecJunitFormatter --out reports/rspec.xml''</span>
      }
      post {
        always {
          junit <span class="s">''reports/rspec.xml''</span>
        }
      }
    }
    stage(<span class="s">''Notify DevTeam''</span>) {
      steps {
        script {
          <span class="k">def</span> result = currentBuild.result ?: <span class="s">''SUCCESS''</span>
          sh <span class="s">"""
            curl -X POST ${DEVTEAM_URL}/webhooks/jenkins \\
              -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' \\
              -H ''X-Jenkins-Token: ${DEVTEAM_TOKEN}'' \\
              -d ''{"build_number":"${BUILD_NUMBER}","status":"${result}",
                   "branch":"${GIT_BRANCH}","commit":"${GIT_COMMIT}"}''
          """</span>
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

      <h2>Jenkins Callback Handler in Rails</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="c"># app/controllers/webhooks_controller.rb (jenkins action)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">jenkins</span>
  token = request.headers[<span class="s">"X-Jenkins-Token"</span>]
  <span class="k">return</span> head :unauthorized <span class="k">unless</span> token == <span class="m">ENV</span>[<span class="s">"JENKINS_WEBHOOK_TOKEN"</span>]

  data = <span class="m">JSON</span>.parse(request.raw_post)
  ci_run = <span class="m">CiRun</span>.find_or_initialize_by(build_number: data[<span class="s">"build_number"</span>])
  ci_run.update!(
    status:     data[<span class="s">"status"</span>] == <span class="s">"SUCCESS"</span> ? :passed : :failed,
    commit_sha: data[<span class="s">"commit"</span>],
    branch_name: data[<span class="s">"branch"</span>],
    finished_at: <span class="m">Time</span>.current
  )
  head :ok
<span class="k">end</span>
</code></pre>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
        <p><strong>Docker install:</strong> <code>docker run -p 8080:8080 -v jenkins_home:/var/jenkins_home jenkins/jenkins:lts-jdk17</code>. First-run unlock password is in <code>/var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 3 — DEPLOYMENTS ══════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="deployments">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon blue">🚀</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 3</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Deployments — Kamal</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>Kamal (formerly MRSK) is a deployment tool by Basecamp that packages the Rails app into a Docker image and deploys it to one or more remote servers with zero-downtime rolling restarts using Traefik as a reverse proxy.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card blue">
          <div class="tool-logo">🚀</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Kamal 2</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Zero-Downtime Deployer</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Ships a Docker image to production servers, health-checks before switching traffic, and rolls back automatically on failure. No Kubernetes needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card green">
          <div class="tool-logo">🔀</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Traefik</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Reverse Proxy / Load Balancer</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Kamal manages a Traefik instance on the server to route traffic, handle TLS termination, and perform blue/green container swaps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>config/deploy.yml</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">yaml</span><code><span class="c"># config/deploy.yml</span>
service: devteam-hub
image: your-registry/devteam-hub

servers:
  web:
    - <span class="s">192.168.1.100</span>    <span class="c"># production server IP</span>

registry:
  server: registry.yourcompany.local
  username:
    - <span class="m">KAMAL_REGISTRY_USERNAME</span>
  password:
    - <span class="m">KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD</span>

env:
  clear:
    RAILS_ENV: production
    RAILS_LOG_TO_STDOUT: <span class="s">"true"</span>
    PORT: <span class="n">3000</span>
  secret:
    - RAILS_MASTER_KEY
    - DATABASE_URL
    - GITEA_TOKEN
    - MINIO_ACCESS_KEY
    - MINIO_SECRET_KEY

volumes:
  - <span class="s">"devteam_storage:/rails/storage"</span>

proxy:
  ssl: true
  host: devteam.yourcompany.local
</code></pre>

      <h2>Deploy Commands</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash</span><code><span class="c"># First-time setup (provisions Traefik, builds image)</span>
kamal setup

<span class="c"># Regular deploy</span>
kamal deploy

<span class="c"># Rollback to previous version</span>
kamal rollback

<span class="c"># Run a one-off command on server</span>
kamal app exec -i "bin/rails db:migrate"

<span class="c"># Live logs</span>
kamal logs -f
</code></pre>

      <div class="callout success">
        <span class="callout-icon">✅</span>
        <p>Kamal is included in Rails 8 by default. The <code>config/deploy.yml</code> and <code>Dockerfile</code> are generated by <code>rails new</code>. Run <code>gem install kamal</code> on your dev machine if deploying from outside the project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 4 — VIDEO ════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="video">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon teal">📹</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 4</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Video Calls — Jitsi Meet</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>Jitsi Meet is a fully open-source, self-hostable video conferencing platform. DevTeam Hub embeds Jitsi rooms directly into meeting pages via an iframe. Each meeting generates a unique room name, and developers can join with one click.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card teal">
          <div class="tool-logo">📹</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Jitsi Meet</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Video Conferencing</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">WebRTC-based video calls. Can use the public <code>meet.jit.si</code> server for free, or deploy your own Jitsi instance on any Linux server.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card blue">
          <div class="tool-logo">🔧</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Jitsi External API</div>
          <div class="tool-type">JavaScript SDK</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">The <code>external_api.js</code> library allows embedding a Jitsi conference in any webpage with full event handling — join/leave, recording, chat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Meeting Model — jitsi_url</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="c"># app/models/meeting.rb</span>
<span class="k">class</span> <span class="m">Meeting</span> &lt; <span class="m">ApplicationRecord</span>
  <span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">jitsi_url</span>
    <span class="s">"https://meet.jit.si/#{jitsi_room}"</span> <span class="k">if</span> jitsi_room.present?
  <span class="k">end</span>

  before_create <span class="k">do</span>
    self.jitsi_room ||= <span class="s">"devteam-#{SecureRandom.hex(6)}"</span>
  <span class="k">end</span>
<span class="k">end</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>Embedded Jitsi Room (ERB)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">erb</span><code>&lt;%<span class="c"># app/views/meetings/show.html.erb</span> %&gt;
&lt;div id=<span class="s">"jitsi-container"</span> style=<span class="s">"height:580px;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden"</span>&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;script src=<span class="s">"https://meet.jit.si/external_api.js"</span>&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
  const api = new JitsiMeetExternalAPI(<span class="s">"meet.jit.si"</span>, {
    roomName:   <span class="s">"&lt;%= @meeting.jitsi_room %&gt;"</span>,
    parentNode: document.getElementById(<span class="s">"jitsi-container"</span>),
    userInfo:   { displayName: <span class="s">"&lt;%= current_user.display_name %&gt;"</span> },
    configOverwrite: { startWithAudioMuted: true },
    interfaceConfigOverwrite: {
      TOOLBAR_BUTTONS: [<span class="s">''microphone''</span>, <span class="s">''camera''</span>, <span class="s">''chat''</span>, <span class="s">''recording''</span>, <span class="s">''hangup''</span>]
    }
  });

  api.addEventListener(<span class="s">''videoConferenceLeft''</span>, () =&gt; {
    fetch(<span class="s">"&lt;%= end_meeting_meeting_path(@meeting) %&gt;"</span>,
      { method: <span class="s">''POST''</span>, headers: { <span class="s">''X-CSRF-Token''</span>: document.querySelector(<span class="s">''[name="csrf-token"]''</span>).content }});
  });
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

      <h2>Self-hosted Jitsi (Docker Compose)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash</span><code><span class="c"># Clone and configure Jitsi Docker</span>
git clone https://github.com/jitsi/docker-jitsi-meet
cd docker-jitsi-meet
cp env.example .env
<span class="c"># Generate secrets</span>
./gen-passwords.sh
<span class="c"># Point your DNS: video.yourcompany.local → server IP</span>
docker compose up -d
</code></pre>

      <p>Then update your Meeting model to use <code>"video.yourcompany.local"</code> instead of <code>"meet.jit.si"</code>.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 5 — S3 / MINIO ═══════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="s3">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon yellow">🗄️</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 5</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">On-Prem S3 — MinIO</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>MinIO is a high-performance, S3-compatible object storage server you can run entirely on-prem. Rails Active Storage supports it out of the box as an S3 provider — no AWS account needed.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card orange">
          <div class="tool-logo">🗄️</div>
          <div class="tool-name">MinIO</div>
          <div class="tool-type">S3-Compatible Object Storage</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Runs on Linux, Windows, or macOS. Exposes the full AWS S3 API — presigned URLs, multipart uploads, lifecycle policies, bucket policies, and a web UI on port 9001.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card green">
          <div class="tool-logo">📎</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Active Storage</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Rails File Attachment Layer</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Rails built-in. Attach files to any model, serve via redirect or direct URL. Switch backend (local disk → MinIO → AWS S3) by changing one config file.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Step 1 — Run MinIO</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash (Docker)</span><code><span class="c"># Run MinIO with Docker</span>
docker run -d \
  --name minio \
  -p 9000:9000 \
  -p 9001:9001 \
  -e <span class="v">MINIO_ROOT_USER</span>=<span class="s">minioadmin</span> \
  -e <span class="v">MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD</span>=<span class="s">minioadmin123</span> \
  -v minio_data:/data \
  quay.io/minio/minio server /data --console-address <span class="s">":9001"</span>
</code></pre>

      <p>Open <code>http://localhost:9001</code>, log in, and create a bucket named <code>devteam-storage</code>.</p>

      <h2>Step 2 — Gemfile</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="c"># Gemfile</span>
gem <span class="s">"aws-sdk-s3"</span>, require: false  <span class="c"># used by Active Storage S3 service</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>Step 3 — storage.yml</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">yaml</span><code><span class="c"># config/storage.yml</span>
minio:
  service: S3
  access_key_id:     &lt;%= ENV["MINIO_ACCESS_KEY"] %&gt;
  secret_access_key: &lt;%= ENV["MINIO_SECRET_KEY"] %&gt;
  region:   us-east-1          <span class="c"># MinIO ignores region but needs a value</span>
  bucket:   devteam-storage
  endpoint: <span class="s">"http://minio.local:9000"</span>
  force_path_style: true       <span class="c"># required for MinIO (no virtual-hosted-style)</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>Step 4 — environments/production.rb</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code>config.active_storage.service = :minio
</code></pre>

      <h2>Step 5 — Environment Variables</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash</span><code><span class="v">MINIO_ACCESS_KEY</span>=<span class="s">minioadmin</span>
<span class="v">MINIO_SECRET_KEY</span>=<span class="s">minioadmin123</span>
<span class="v">MINIO_ENDPOINT</span>=<span class="s">http://minio.local:9000</span>
<span class="v">MINIO_BUCKET</span>=<span class="s">devteam-storage</span>
</code></pre>

      <h2>Using Active Storage in a Model</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">ruby</span><code><span class="k">class</span> <span class="m">Document</span> &lt; <span class="m">ApplicationRecord</span>
  has_one_attached :file           <span class="c"># single file</span>
  has_many_attached :attachments   <span class="c"># multiple files</span>
<span class="k">end</span>

<span class="c"># In a form:</span>
<span class="c"># &lt;%= f.file_field :file %&gt;</span>

<span class="c"># Generate a presigned download URL (works with MinIO):</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="m">download_url</span>
  rails_blob_url(file, disposition: <span class="s">"attachment"</span>) <span class="k">if</span> file.attached?
<span class="k">end</span>
</code></pre>

      <div class="callout info">
        <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
        <p><strong>CORS for direct uploads:</strong> Configure MinIO bucket CORS policy to allow <code>PUT</code> from your Rails app domain if using Active Storage direct uploads.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Chart -->
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <div class="chart-title">Storage Backend Comparison</div>
        <canvas id="storageChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 6 — WINDOWS SERVER ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="windows">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon gray">🪟</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 6</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Running on Windows Server</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>Running the full stack on Windows Server is best achieved via Docker Desktop (WSL2 backend) or Docker Engine on Windows Server 2019/2022. All services — Rails, Gitea, Jenkins, MinIO, Jitsi — run as Docker containers managed by Docker Compose.</p>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
        <p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Windows Server 2022 with Docker Engine (no Desktop license required for server SKUs). Enable Hyper-V and WSL2 features for best performance.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Enable Docker on Windows Server 2022</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">powershell</span><code><span class="c"># Run as Administrator</span>
<span class="c"># Enable required Windows features</span>
<span class="m">Install-WindowsFeature</span> -Name Hyper-V, Containers -IncludeManagementTools -Restart

<span class="c"># Install Docker Engine</span>
<span class="m">Invoke-WebRequest</span> -UseBasicParsing <span class="s">"https://get.docker.com"</span> -o get-docker.ps1
<span class="m">.\get-docker.ps1</span>

<span class="c"># Or via winget</span>
winget install Docker.DockerDesktop

<span class="c"># Start Docker service</span>
<span class="m">Start-Service</span> docker
<span class="m">Set-Service</span> -Name docker -StartupType Automatic
</code></pre>

      <h2>Full Stack docker-compose.windows.yml</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">yaml</span><code>version: <span class="s">"3.9"</span>

services:

  <span class="c"># ── Rails App ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
  web:
    build: .
    image: devteam-hub:latest
    ports: [<span class="s">"5000:3000"</span>]
    environment:
      RAILS_ENV:          production
      RAILS_MASTER_KEY:   ${RAILS_MASTER_KEY}
      MINIO_ACCESS_KEY:   ${MINIO_ACCESS_KEY}
      MINIO_SECRET_KEY:   ${MINIO_SECRET_KEY}
      GITEA_URL:          http://gitea:3000
      GITEA_TOKEN:        ${GITEA_TOKEN}
      JENKINS_URL:        http://jenkins:8080
    volumes:
      - rails_storage:/rails/storage
    depends_on: [gitea, minio]
    restart: unless-stopped

  <span class="c"># ── Gitea ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
  gitea:
    image: gitea/gitea:latest
    ports: [<span class="s">"3001:3000"</span>, <span class="s">"222:22"</span>]
    volumes:
      - gitea_data:/data
    restart: unless-stopped

  <span class="c"># ── Jenkins ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
  jenkins:
    image: jenkins/jenkins:lts-jdk17
    ports: [<span class="s">"8080:8080"</span>]
    volumes:
      - jenkins_home:/var/jenkins_home
    restart: unless-stopped

  <span class="c"># ── MinIO (S3) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
  minio:
    image: quay.io/minio/minio
    command: server /data --console-address ":9001"
    ports: [<span class="s">"9000:9000"</span>, <span class="s">"9001:9001"</span>]
    environment:
      MINIO_ROOT_USER:     ${MINIO_ACCESS_KEY}
      MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD: ${MINIO_SECRET_KEY}
    volumes:
      - minio_data:/data
    restart: unless-stopped

  <span class="c"># ── Jitsi (optional — self-hosted video) ──────────────────────────────────</span>
  jitsi-web:
    image: jitsi/web:stable
    ports: [<span class="s">"8443:443"</span>]
    env_file: .jitsi.env
    volumes:
      - jitsi_config:/config
    restart: unless-stopped

volumes:
  rails_storage:
  gitea_data:
  jenkins_home:
  minio_data:
  jitsi_config:
</code></pre>

      <h2>Start Everything</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">powershell</span><code><span class="c"># Create .env file with secrets</span>
@<span class="s">"
RAILS_MASTER_KEY=your_master_key_here
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
MINIO_SECRET_KEY=supersecret123
GITEA_TOKEN=your_gitea_token
"</span>@ | <span class="m">Set-Content</span> .env

<span class="c"># Build and start</span>
docker compose -f docker-compose.windows.yml up -d --build

<span class="c"># Run migrations</span>
docker compose exec web bin/rails db:migrate

<span class="c"># Check logs</span>
docker compose logs -f web
</code></pre>

      <div class="callout info">
        <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
        <p><strong>IIS Reverse Proxy (optional):</strong> Install the <em>Application Request Routing</em> module in IIS and configure a reverse proxy from <code>port 80/443</code> to <code>localhost:5000</code> for production SSL termination via Windows certificates.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 7 — DOCKER ════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="docker">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon blue">🐳</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 7</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Docker Setup — Rails App</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Production Dockerfile (Rails)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">dockerfile</span><code><span class="c"># ── Stage 1: Build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
FROM ruby:3.4.5-slim AS build

WORKDIR /rails

<span class="c"># Install build dependencies</span>
RUN apt-get update -qq &amp;&amp; apt-get install -y \
    build-essential git libsqlite3-dev curl nodejs npm &amp;&amp; \
    npm install -g yarn &amp;&amp; rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY Gemfile Gemfile.lock ./
RUN bundle config set --local deployment true &amp;&amp; \
    bundle config set --local without "development test" &amp;&amp; \
    bundle install --jobs 4

COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci

COPY . .

<span class="c"># Precompile assets &amp; JS</span>
RUN npm run build &amp;&amp; npm run build:css
RUN SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY=1 bin/rails assets:precompile

<span class="c"># ── Stage 2: Runtime ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
FROM ruby:3.4.5-slim AS runtime

WORKDIR /rails

RUN apt-get update -qq &amp;&amp; apt-get install -y libsqlite3-0 curl &amp;&amp; \
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY --from=build /usr/local/bundle /usr/local/bundle
COPY --from=build /rails /rails

<span class="c"># Non-root user for security</span>
RUN useradd -m -s /bin/bash rails &amp;&amp; chown -R rails:rails /rails
USER rails

EXPOSE 3000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --start-period=40s \
  CMD curl -f http://localhost:3000/up || exit 1

ENTRYPOINT ["./bin/docker-entrypoint"]
CMD ["./bin/rails", "server", "-b", "0.0.0.0", "-p", "3000"]
</code></pre>

      <h2>bin/docker-entrypoint</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">bash</span><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -e

<span class="c"># Run migrations on startup</span>
if [ "$RAILS_ENV" = "production" ]; then
  bundle exec rails db:migrate 2&gt;/dev/null || true
fi

exec "${@}"
</code></pre>

      <h2>Development docker-compose.yml</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">yaml</span><code>version: <span class="s">"3.9"</span>
services:
  web:
    build:
      context: .
      target: build          <span class="c"># use build stage for dev (has npm etc.)</span>
    command: bin/rails server -b 0.0.0.0 -p 3000
    ports: [<span class="s">"5000:3000"</span>]
    volumes:
      - .:/rails
      - bundle_cache:/usr/local/bundle
    environment:
      RAILS_ENV:   development
      GITEA_URL:   http://gitea:3000
      MINIO_ENDPOINT: http://minio:9000
    depends_on: [minio, gitea]

  minio:
    image: quay.io/minio/minio
    command: server /data --console-address ":9001"
    ports: [<span class="s">"9000:9000"</span>, <span class="s">"9001:9001"</span>]
    volumes: [minio_data:/data]
    environment:
      MINIO_ROOT_USER: devteam
      MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD: devteam123

  gitea:
    image: gitea/gitea:latest
    ports: [<span class="s">"3001:3000"</span>, <span class="s">"222:22"</span>]
    volumes: [gitea_data:/data]

volumes:
  bundle_cache:
  minio_data:
  gitea_data:
</code></pre>
    </div>

    <!-- ═════════════════════════ CHAPTER 8 — ASP.NET DOCKER ════════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="docker-aspnet">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon purple">🔷</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 8</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">ASP.NET Project — Dockerfile</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>If you have a companion ASP.NET application (e.g. a Windows service, print server, or API), here is a production-ready multi-stage Dockerfile for both ASP.NET Core Web API and a Worker Service, plus how to connect it to MinIO and the DevTeam Hub API.</p>

      <h2>ASP.NET Core Web API Dockerfile</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">dockerfile</span><code><span class="c"># ── Stage 1: Restore &amp; Build ───────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src

<span class="c"># Copy csproj and restore</span>
COPY ["MyApi/MyApi.csproj", "MyApi/"]
RUN dotnet restore "MyApi/MyApi.csproj"

<span class="c"># Copy all source and build</span>
COPY . .
WORKDIR /src/MyApi
RUN dotnet build -c Release -o /app/build

<span class="c"># ── Stage 2: Publish ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
FROM build AS publish
RUN dotnet publish -c Release -o /app/publish \
    /p:UseAppHost=false

<span class="c"># ── Stage 3: Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:8.0 AS final
WORKDIR /app

<span class="c"># Non-root user</span>
RUN adduser --disabled-password --gecos "" appuser
USER appuser

COPY --from=publish /app/publish .

EXPOSE 8080
EXPOSE 8081

HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s CMD \
  curl -f http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1

ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "MyApi.dll"]
</code></pre>

      <h2>ASP.NET Worker Service Dockerfile (Windows Service)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">dockerfile</span><code><span class="c"># Suitable for a print server, background processor, or Windows Service</span>
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY ["PrintServer/PrintServer.csproj", "PrintServer/"]
RUN dotnet restore "PrintServer/PrintServer.csproj"
COPY . .
WORKDIR /src/PrintServer
RUN dotnet publish -c Release -o /app/publish

FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/runtime:8.0 AS final
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/publish .
ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "PrintServer.dll"]
</code></pre>

      <h2>Connecting ASP.NET to MinIO (AWSSDK.S3)</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">csharp</span><code><span class="c">// Program.cs</span>
<span class="k">using</span> <span class="m">Amazon.S3</span>;

builder.Services.AddSingleton&lt;<span class="m">IAmazonS3</span>&gt;(_ =&gt;
{
    <span class="k">var</span> config = <span class="k">new</span> <span class="m">AmazonS3Config</span>
    {
        ServiceURL       = <span class="m">Environment</span>.GetEnvironmentVariable(<span class="s">"MINIO_ENDPOINT"</span>),
        ForcePathStyle   = <span class="k">true</span>,   <span class="c">// required for MinIO</span>
        UseHttp          = <span class="k">true</span>
    };
    <span class="k">return new</span> <span class="m">AmazonS3Client</span>(
        <span class="m">Environment</span>.GetEnvironmentVariable(<span class="s">"MINIO_ACCESS_KEY"</span>),
        <span class="m">Environment</span>.GetEnvironmentVariable(<span class="s">"MINIO_SECRET_KEY"</span>),
        config);
});
</code></pre>

      <pre><span class="lang-label">csharp</span><code><span class="c">// FileService.cs — upload a file to MinIO</span>
<span class="k">public class</span> <span class="m">FileService</span>(<span class="m">IAmazonS3</span> s3)
{
    <span class="k">public async Task</span>&lt;<span class="k">string</span>&gt; UploadAsync(<span class="m">Stream</span> stream, <span class="k">string</span> key)
    {
        <span class="k">await</span> s3.PutObjectAsync(<span class="k">new</span> <span class="m">PutObjectRequest</span>
        {
            BucketName  = <span class="s">"devteam-storage"</span>,
            Key         = key,
            InputStream = stream,
            ContentType = <span class="s">"application/octet-stream"</span>
        });
        <span class="k">return</span> <span class="s">$"http://minio.local:9000/devteam-storage/{key}"</span>;
    }
}
</code></pre>

      <h2>Connecting ASP.NET to DevTeam Hub API</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">csharp</span><code><span class="c">// DevTeamClient.cs — call the DevTeam Hub REST API</span>
<span class="k">public class</span> <span class="m">DevTeamClient</span>(<span class="m">HttpClient</span> http)
{
    <span class="k">public async Task</span> UpdateTicketAsync(<span class="k">int</span> ticketId, <span class="k">string</span> status)
    {
        <span class="k">var</span> payload = <span class="m">JsonSerializer</span>.Serialize(<span class="k">new</span> { ticket = <span class="k">new</span> { status } });
        http.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add(<span class="s">"X-Api-Token"</span>,
            <span class="m">Environment</span>.GetEnvironmentVariable(<span class="s">"DEVTEAM_API_TOKEN"</span>));
        <span class="k">await</span> http.PutAsync(
            <span class="s">$"/api/v1/tickets/{ticketId}"</span>,
            <span class="k">new</span> <span class="m">StringContent</span>(payload, <span class="m">Encoding</span>.UTF8, <span class="s">"application/json"</span>));
    }
}

<span class="c">// Register in Program.cs</span>
builder.Services.AddHttpClient&lt;<span class="m">DevTeamClient</span>&gt;(c =&gt;
    c.BaseAddress = <span class="k">new</span> <span class="m">Uri</span>(<span class="m">Environment</span>.GetEnvironmentVariable(<span class="s">"DEVTEAM_URL"</span>)));
</code></pre>

      <h2>docker-compose snippet — side by side with Rails</h2>
      <pre><span class="lang-label">yaml</span><code>services:
  web:            <span class="c"># Rails app (see Chapter 7)</span>
    build: .
    ports: [<span class="s">"5000:3000"</span>]

  my-api:         <span class="c"># ASP.NET Core API</span>
    build:
      context: ./MyApi
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    ports: [<span class="s">"8080:8080"</span>]
    environment:
      MINIO_ENDPOINT:   http://minio:9000
      MINIO_ACCESS_KEY: devteam
      MINIO_SECRET_KEY: devteam123
      DEVTEAM_URL:      http://web:3000
      DEVTEAM_API_TOKEN: ${DEVTEAM_API_TOKEN}
    depends_on: [web, minio]

  print-server:   <span class="c"># ASP.NET Worker Service</span>
    build:
      context: ./PrintServer
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    environment:
      MINIO_ENDPOINT:   http://minio:9000
    depends_on: [minio]
</code></pre>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════ CHAPTER 9 — AUTOMATED TESTING ════════════════ -->
    <div class="chapter" id="testing-overview">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-icon" style="background:#fef9c3">🧪</div>
        <div>
          <div class="chapter-num">Chapter 9</div>
          <div class="chapter-title">Automated Testing Strategy</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>DevTeam Hub manages projects across multiple technology stacks. This chapter recommends a consistent <strong>Behaviour-Driven Development (BDD)</strong> approach using Cucumber-style feature files (Gherkin) for every stack, so product and QA teams can read and write tests in plain English regardless of the underlying technology.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card green">
          <div class="tool-logo">💎</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Cucumber + Capybara</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Rails / Ruby</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Native Cucumber for Ruby. Capybara drives a real browser via the Selenium or Playwright driver. Already present in this project''s <code>features/</code> directory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card purple">
          <div class="tool-logo">🔷</div>
          <div class="tool-name">SpecFlow + Playwright</div>
          <div class="tool-type">ASP.NET Core (.NET 6+)</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">SpecFlow translates <code>.feature</code> files into xUnit/NUnit tests. Microsoft.Playwright provides fast, reliable browser automation across Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card orange">
          <div class="tool-logo">🪟</div>
          <div class="tool-name">SpecFlow + Selenium</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Legacy .NET (4.x / .NET Framework)</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">SpecFlow works on .NET Framework 4.6.1+. Selenium WebDriver is the standard browser automation library for legacy stacks — no modern async runtime needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card blue">
          <div class="tool-logo">🟡</div>
          <div class="tool-name">Cucumber.js + Playwright</div>
          <div class="tool-type">Bun / Node.js</div>
          <p class="tool-desc">Cucumber.js brings Gherkin feature files to the JavaScript ecosystem. Paired with Playwright''s Node.js API it gives the fastest cross-browser headless tests for any Bun or Node app.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Testing Pyramid at a Glance</h2>
      <div class="arch-diagram">
        <svg width="600" height="260" viewBox="0 0 600 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">
