      <div class="body grid g-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1) Print Server / TDI (.NET + VB)</h3>
          <p><strong>Focus:</strong> queue stability, timeout recovery, locale defaults, printer profile behavior.</p>
          <pre>Feature: Printer network fault recovery
  Scenario: Job fails cleanly after timeout retry budget
    Given a running print queue
    When printer connectivity is lost mid-transfer
    Then the system retries according to policy
    And the job ends in Failed state with reason code</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2) TDI2 (ASP.NET Core + RabbitMQ)</h3>
          <p><strong>Focus:</strong> message workflows, concurrency safety, dead-letter handling.</p>
          <pre>Feature: Dead-letter routing
  Scenario: Invalid payload is moved to DLQ
    Given queue orders.inbound receives malformed payload
    When consumer validation runs
    Then message is rejected
    And message appears in orders.dlq with diagnostics</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3) Digital Internet Services (Vue + NestJS)</h3>
          <p><strong>Focus:</strong> customer API contract, auth flows, UI journey from portal to support ticket.</p>
          <pre>Feature: Customer support submission
  Scenario: Portal user opens a support ticket
    Given authenticated customer "Acme"
    When they submit issue "Connection timeout"
    Then ticket is created
    And dashboard shows status Open</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>4) Work Management System (Next.js + Bun)</h3>
          <p><strong>Focus:</strong> workflow state transitions, Kanban consistency, search/index correctness.</p>
          <pre>Feature: Kanban state transition
  Scenario: Move item from In Progress to Review
    Given task T-431 in In Progress
    When user drags task to Review
    Then task status becomes In Review
    And audit activity is recorded</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>5) DevTeam Hub (Rails)</h3>
          <p><strong>Focus:</strong> reports, notifications, integrations, ticket-to-branch behavior.</p>
          <pre>Feature: Assignment creates branch and notification
  Scenario: Assign ticket to developer
    Given ticket #88 exists in project "TDI2"
    When assignee is set to "noam@devteam.local"
    Then a branch is generated for that ticket
    And assignee receives notification with branch command</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>UI example with Playwright (shared pattern)</h3>
          <pre>test(''create ticket and verify list update'', async ({ page }) =&gt; {
  await page.goto(''/customers/1/tickets/new'');
  await page.fill(''[name="title"]'', ''Printer timeout on floor 2'');
  await page.click(''button:has-text("Create")'');
  await expect(page.locator(''text=Printer timeout on floor 2'')).toBeVisible();
});</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
