  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Code Review &amp; Approval in CI</h1>
    <p>A comprehensive evaluation of automated code review tools for our multi-language stack — with emphasis on on-premises deployment, AI-assisted reviews, and CI pipeline integration.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- Requirements                                        -->
  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="section" id="requirements">
    <h2><span class="icon">📋</span> Requirements</h2>
    <p>Based on our team''s stack and infrastructure constraints, the ideal code review/approval tool must meet:</p>

    <h3>Language Coverage</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>Languages / Frameworks</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Print Server / TDI</td><td>C# (.NET 4.8.1), VB.NET, WinForms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>TDI2</td><td>C# (ASP.NET Core 10), Razor Pages, JavaScript, SQL</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Digital Internet Services</td><td>TypeScript, Vue 3, JavaScript, NestJS (Node.js), SQL</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Work Management System</td><td>TypeScript, Next.js 16, Bun, SQL</td></tr>
        <tr><td>DevTeam Hub</td><td>Ruby, Rails 8.1, JavaScript (Stimulus), ERB, HTML, CSS, SQL</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><strong>Languages needed:</strong> Ruby, C#, VB.NET, TypeScript, JavaScript, SQL, HTML/CSS, ERB, Razor Pages</p>

    <h3>Must-Have Requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On-premises deployment</strong> — All code stays on our internal network. No source code sent to external clouds.</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-language support</strong> — Ruby, C#, TypeScript, JavaScript, VB.NET at minimum.</li>
      <li><strong>CI integration</strong> — Runs as a step in Jenkins pipelines and GitHub Actions.</li>
      <li><strong>Gitea compatibility</strong> — Posts review comments on Gitea pull requests via API.</li>
      <li><strong>Static analysis</strong> — SAST (security), linting, code smells, complexity metrics.</li>
      <li><strong>PR gate</strong> — Can block merge if quality thresholds are not met.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Nice-to-Have</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>AI-powered review suggestions (on-prem LLM or self-hosted AI)</li>
      <li>Historical quality trends and dashboards</li>
      <li>Custom rules per project/language</li>
      <li>IDE integration (VS Code, Visual Studio)</li>
      <li>Low resource footprint (we run on a single Windows Server)</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- Tool Landscape                                      -->
  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="section" id="landscape">
    <h2><span class="icon">🗺️</span> Tool Landscape</h2>
    <p>We evaluated tools in two categories: <strong>traditional static analysis</strong> (rule-based) and <strong>AI-powered review</strong> (LLM-based).</p>

    <h3>Category A: Static Analysis &amp; Quality Gates</h3>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="tool-card winner">
        <div class="name">SonarQube</div>
        <div class="tagline">The industry standard for continuous code quality</div>
        <span class="badge badge-teal">★ RECOMMENDED</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>30+ languages (all of ours covered)</li>
          <li>Community Edition = free, on-prem</li>
          <li>Quality Gates block merges</li>
          <li>OWASP Top 10 security rules</li>
          <li>Docker deployment</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="name">CodeClimate</div>
        <div class="tagline">Quality metrics and maintainability scores</div>
        <span class="badge badge-orange">Cloud-only</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>Ruby, JS, TS, C# support</li>
          <li>No on-prem option</li>
          <li>$15/user/month</li>
          <li>Good GitHub integration</li>
          <li>❌ No VB.NET or Razor</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="name">Codacy</div>
        <div class="tagline">Automated code reviews with dashboards</div>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">Self-hosted available</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>40+ languages</li>
          <li>Self-hosted ($$$)</li>
          <li>$15/user/month (cloud)</li>
          <li>Gitea integration via API</li>
          <li>Heavier than SonarQube</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Category B: Lightweight / CLI-Based</h3>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="name">MegaLinter</div>
        <div class="tagline">All-in-one linting aggregator (50+ linters)</div>
        <span class="badge badge-green">Free &amp; open source</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>Aggregates existing linters</li>
          <li>Docker-based, fully on-prem</li>
          <li>Gitea PR commenting</li>
          <li>Free forever</li>
          <li>No quality gate dashboard</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="name">Reviewdog</div>
        <div class="tagline">Post linter results as PR review comments</div>
        <span class="badge badge-green">Free &amp; open source</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>Language-agnostic (wraps any linter)</li>
          <li>Gitea support built-in</li>
          <li>Only posts comments, no analysis</li>
          <li>Pairs well with SonarQube</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="name">Semgrep</div>
        <div class="tagline">Fast, open-source SAST with custom rules</div>
        <span class="badge badge-green">Free OSS / Paid cloud</span>
        <ul style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.88rem;">
          <li>Focus on security (SAST)</li>
          <li>Ruby, C#, TS, JS support</li>
          <li>Custom rules via YAML</li>
          <li>CLI-only (no dashboard)</li>
          <li>❌ No VB.NET support</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

