  <div class="section" id="ai-solutions">
    <h2><span class="icon">🤖</span> AI-Powered Code Review Solutions</h2>

    <h3>Cloud-Based AI Reviewers</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Model</th><th>Languages</th><th>On-Prem</th><th>Pricing</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>GitHub Copilot Code Review</strong></td>
          <td>GPT-4o</td>
          <td>All major</td>
          <td>❌ Cloud only</td>
          <td>$19/user/mo (Business)<br>$39/user/mo (Enterprise)</td>
          <td>Native GitHub integration. No Gitea support. Source code sent to Microsoft.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>CodeRabbit</strong></td>
          <td>GPT-4 / Claude</td>
          <td>All major</td>
          <td>❌ Cloud only</td>
          <td>Free (OSS)<br>$15/user/mo (Pro)</td>
          <td>Great reviews. Gitea support planned but not available. Code sent to cloud.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Sourcery</strong></td>
          <td>Proprietary AI</td>
          <td>Python, JS, TS</td>
          <td>❌ Cloud only</td>
          <td>Free (OSS)<br>$30/user/mo (Team)</td>
          <td>❌ No Ruby, C#, VB.NET. Python-focused.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer</strong></td>
          <td>Amazon ML</td>
          <td>Java, Python, JS</td>
          <td>❌ AWS only</td>
          <td>$0.75/100 lines</td>
          <td>❌ No Ruby, C#, VB.NET. AWS-locked.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="bad">
      <strong>❌ Problem with cloud AI:</strong> All cloud-based AI reviewers send your source code to external servers. This violates our on-premises requirement. None of them natively support Gitea.
    </div>

    <h3>Self-Hosted AI Review (On-Prem)</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Approach</th><th>Model</th><th>Languages</th><th>On-Prem</th><th>Cost</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Ollama + Custom Review Agent</strong></td>
          <td>CodeLlama 34B, DeepSeek Coder V2, Qwen2.5-Coder</td>
          <td>All major</td>
          <td>✅ Fully on-prem</td>
          <td>Free (hardware cost only)</td>
          <td>Run open-source code LLMs locally. Requires GPU (16+ GB VRAM). We build a review script that sends diffs to the local LLM.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>SonarQube + AI CodeFix</strong><br>(Developer Edition)</td>
          <td>Sonar proprietary AI</td>
          <td>All SonarQube langs</td>
          <td>✅ On-prem server</td>
          <td>From $150/yr (Dev Ed)</td>
          <td>AI-generated fix suggestions for detected issues. Integrated into the SonarQube workflow. AI runs on Sonar''s edge, but only sends issue context (not full source).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>LiteLLM Proxy + Review Script</strong></td>
          <td>Any (OpenAI, Anthropic, local)</td>
          <td>All</td>
          <td>✅ Self-hosted proxy</td>
          <td>Free proxy + model costs</td>
          <td>Unified API proxy. Route to local Ollama in dev, or pay-per-token API in prod. Flexible but requires custom scripting.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="rec">
      <strong>🟣 Recommended AI approach:</strong> Start with <strong>SonarQube Community Edition</strong> for deterministic analysis, then add <strong>Ollama + a review script</strong> for AI-assisted suggestions on complex PRs. This gives us the best of both worlds — reliable quality gates + intelligent suggestions — fully on-prem.
    </div>
  </div>

