<div class="main">

<!-- ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="hero">
  <h1>Unified <span>Application Logging</span><br>Recommendation &amp; Implementation</h1>
  <p>Centralised, structured log management across all 5 managed projects — fully on-premises, integrated with Jenkins CI, Gitea, and DevTeam Hub.</p>
  <div class="hero-tags">
    <span class="hero-tag">Grafana Loki</span>
    <span class="hero-tag">Promtail</span>
    <span class="hero-tag">Grafana</span>
    <span class="hero-tag">Structured JSON Logs</span>
    <span class="hero-tag">On-Premises</span>
    <span class="hero-tag">Zero Cost</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 1. PROBLEM STATEMENT                                                -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="problem" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">1. Current Logging Issues</div>
  <div class="section-sub">Each application logs differently — no unified format, no central storage, no cross-app correlation.</div>

  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>🔴 Fragmented Formats</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;">Rails logs plain text, .NET uses structured EventLog, NestJS uses Winston JSON, Next.js uses console.log. No common schema — impossible to search across apps.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>🔴 No Central Storage</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;">Logs live on each server''s filesystem. SSH required to read them. Log rotation deletes old entries. No searchable archive.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>🔴 No Correlation</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;">No request IDs, trace IDs, or correlation tokens flow between services. Debugging cross-app issues requires manual timestamp matching.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <h3>Current Logging Per Application</h3>
    <table class="styled">
      <thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Language</th><th>Current Logging</th><th>Format</th><th>Storage</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>DevTeam Hub</td><td>Ruby (Rails 8.1)</td><td>ActiveSupport::TaggedLogging → STDOUT</td><td>Plain text</td><td>Docker stdout / log/development.log</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Print Server / TDI</td><td>C# / VB.NET (.NET 4.8.1)</td><td>NLog / EventLog</td><td>Mixed text</td><td>Windows Event Log / file</td></tr>
        <tr><td>TDI2</td><td>C# (ASP.NET Core 10)</td><td>Microsoft.Extensions.Logging</td><td>Structured (partial)</td><td>Console / file</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Digital Internet Services</td><td>TypeScript (NestJS)</td><td>Winston / console</td><td>JSON (partial)</td><td>File / console</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Work Management System</td><td>TypeScript (Next.js 16)</td><td>console.log / pino</td><td>Unstructured</td><td>Console</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 2. REQUIREMENTS                                                     -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="requirements" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">2. Requirements</div>
  <div class="section-sub">What the unified logging solution must provide.</div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Must Have</h3>
      <ul style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;padding-left:1.2rem;">
        <li><strong>On-Premises</strong> — no log data leaves the network</li>
        <li><strong>Unified JSON format</strong> — same schema for all 5 apps</li>
        <li><strong>Central search &amp; query</strong> — search all logs from one UI</li>
        <li><strong>Correlation IDs</strong> — trace requests across services</li>
        <li><strong>CI integration</strong> — Jenkins build logs collected too</li>
        <li><strong>Retention policy</strong> — configurable per environment</li>
        <li><strong>Alerting</strong> — notify on error spikes</li>
        <li><strong>Zero / low cost</strong> — open-source preferred</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Nice to Have</h3>
      <ul style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;padding-left:1.2rem;">
        <li>Dashboard with charts &amp; metrics</li>
        <li>Log-based metrics (error rates, latency percentiles)</li>
        <li>Live tail (real-time streaming)</li>
        <li>API for DevTeam Hub integration</li>
        <li>Windows agent for .NET 4.8.1 apps</li>
        <li>Multi-tenant label isolation per project</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 3. UNIFIED LOG FORMAT                                               -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="format" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">3. Unified Log Format — JSON</div>
  <div class="section-sub">All applications must emit structured JSON logs with these mandatory fields.</div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Standard Log Schema</h3>
    <pre class="code">{
  "timestamp":      "2026-05-24T14:32:01.456Z",   // ISO 8601 UTC
  "level":          "error",                        // debug | info | warn | error | fatal
  "service":        "devteam-hub",                  // app identifier
  "environment":    "production",                   // production | staging | development
  "host":           "srv-web-01",                   // hostname
  "version":        "2.4.1",                        // app version / git SHA
  "correlation_id": "req-a1b2c3d4-e5f6",            // request/trace ID (flows across services)
  "request_id":     "abc-123-def",                  // per-request unique ID
  "user_id":        42,                             // authenticated user (null if anonymous)
  "message":        "Failed to connect to Gitea",   // human-readable message
  "logger":         "GiteaService",                 // class / module / component
  "context": {                                      // arbitrary structured data
    "method":    "POST",
    "path":      "/api/v1/webhooks",
    "status":    502,
    "duration_ms": 3042,
    "error_class": "Faraday::ConnectionFailed",
    "backtrace":   ["app/services/gitea_service.rb:45", "..."]
  }
}</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Mandatory Fields</h3>
      <table class="styled">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>string</td><td>ISO 8601 UTC</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>level</code></td><td>string</td><td>Log severity</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>service</code></td><td>string</td><td>Application name</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td>string</td><td>Deployment environment</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>message</code></td><td>string</td><td>Log message</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>correlation_id</code></td><td>string</td><td>Cross-service trace ID</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Service Identifiers</h3>
      <table class="styled">
        <thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>service value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>DevTeam Hub</td><td><code>devteam-hub</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Print Server</td><td><code>print-server</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>TDI</td><td><code>tdi-legacy</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>TDI2</td><td><code>tdi2</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Digital Internet Services</td><td><code>digital-internet</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Work Management System</td><td><code>work-mgmt</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jenkins CI</td><td><code>jenkins</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 4. TOOL LANDSCAPE                                                   -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="tools" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">4. Log Management Tool Landscape</div>
  <div class="section-sub">Evaluated tools for centralized log aggregation, search, and visualization.</div>

  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card" style="border-left:3px solid var(--teal);">
      <h3>Grafana Loki <span class="badge badge-green">Recommended</span></h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Log aggregation system by Grafana Labs. Does NOT index log content — indexes only labels (service, env, level). Extremely storage-efficient. Native Grafana integration.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-teal">Free &amp; OSS</span>
        <span class="badge badge-teal">On-Prem Docker</span>
        <span class="badge badge-teal">LogQL</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Elasticsearch + Kibana (ELK)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Full-text indexing of all log fields. Extremely powerful search but heavy on resources (RAM, disk). Elastic license changed — OSS fork is OpenSearch.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-orange">Heavy Resources</span>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">Full-Text Search</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Graylog</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Centralized log management with GELF protocol, dashboards, and alerts. Requires Elasticsearch + MongoDB. More complex to deploy.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-orange">3 Services Required</span>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">GELF Protocol</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="three-col" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Fluentd / Fluent Bit</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Log collectors / forwarders. Not storage — they ship logs to a backend (Loki, Elasticsearch, etc.). Fluent Bit is lightweight C agent. Alternative to Promtail.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-teal">Collector Only</span>
        <span class="badge badge-teal">CNCF Project</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Seq (Datalust)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Structured log server optimized for .NET (Serilog). Single-user license free. Excellent for .NET-only shops but limited multi-language support.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-purple">.NET Focused</span>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">Free Single User</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Datadog / Splunk (Cloud)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">Enterprise cloud log platforms. Powerful but expensive and send data off-premises. Not suitable for our on-prem requirement.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.78rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-red">Cloud Only</span>
        <span class="badge badge-red">Expensive</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 5. COMPARISON TABLE                                                 -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="comparison" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">5. Detailed Comparison</div>

  <div class="card">
    <table class="styled">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Criteria</th>
          <th>Grafana Loki</th>
          <th>ELK / OpenSearch</th>
          <th>Graylog</th>
          <th>Seq</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>License</strong></td><td>AGPL-3.0 (free)</td><td>SSPL / Apache-2 (OpenSearch)</td><td>SSPL (free tier)</td><td>Free single-user</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>On-Prem Docker</strong></td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>RAM Required</strong></td><td>256 MB – 1 GB</td><td>4 – 16 GB</td><td>4 – 8 GB</td><td>512 MB – 2 GB</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Storage Efficiency</strong></td><td>⭐ Excellent (no index)</td><td>Poor (full-text index)</td><td>Poor (ES backend)</td><td>Good</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Query Language</strong></td><td>LogQL</td><td>KQL / Lucene</td><td>Search syntax</td><td>SQL-like</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Dashboard</strong></td><td>Grafana (native)</td><td>Kibana / OpenSearch Dashboards</td><td>Built-in</td><td>Built-in</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Alerting</strong></td><td>Grafana Alerting</td><td>ElastAlert / Kibana</td><td>Built-in</td><td>Built-in</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Log Collector</strong></td><td>Promtail / Alloy</td><td>Filebeat / Logstash</td><td>Sidecar / GELF</td><td>Serilog sink</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Multi-Language</strong></td><td>✅ Any (JSON over HTTP)</td><td>✅ Any</td><td>✅ Any</td><td>⚠️ .NET best</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>API</strong></td><td>✅ HTTP Push + LogQL Query</td><td>✅ REST</td><td>✅ REST</td><td>✅ REST</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Live Tail</strong></td><td>✅ WebSocket</td><td>⚠️ Kibana only</td><td>✅ Built-in</td><td>✅ Built-in</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Windows Agent</strong></td><td>✅ Promtail / Alloy</td><td>✅ Winlogbeat</td><td>✅ GELF / Sidecar</td><td>✅ Native</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Complexity</strong></td><td>⭐ Low (2 containers)</td><td>High (3+ containers)</td><td>High (3 containers)</td><td>Low (1 container)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Tool Comparison Radar</div>
      <canvas id="toolRadar" height="300"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Resource Requirements (RAM GB)</div>
      <canvas id="ramChart" height="300"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 6. RECOMMENDATION                                                   -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="recommendation" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">6. Recommendation — Grafana Loki + Promtail + Grafana</div>
  <div class="section-sub">The Grafana stack (often called "PLG" — Promtail, Loki, Grafana) is the best fit for our requirements.</div>

  <div class="highlight">
    <h4>🏆 Why Grafana Loki?</h4>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:.75rem;">
      <ul style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;padding-left:1.2rem;">
        <li><strong>Lightest resource footprint</strong> — doesn''t index content, only labels</li>
        <li><strong>100% on-premises</strong> — Docker Compose, no cloud dependency</li>
        <li><strong>Free &amp; open-source</strong> — AGPL-3.0, no paid tiers needed</li>
        <li><strong>Native Grafana integration</strong> — dashboards, alerts, live tail</li>
      </ul>
      <ul style="font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;padding-left:1.2rem;">
        <li><strong>HTTP Push API</strong> — any language can send logs via POST</li>
        <li><strong>LogQL</strong> — powerful query language with label filtering</li>
        <li><strong>Promtail agent</strong> — works on Linux &amp; Windows</li>
        <li><strong>Already in our ecosystem</strong> — Grafana pairs with Prometheus metrics too</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="pricing" class="cost-box">
    <div>
      <div class="cost-amount">$0 / year</div>
      <div class="cost-label">Grafana Loki + Promtail + Grafana — all free, open-source, self-hosted</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <h3>Stack Components</h3>
    <table class="styled">
      <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th><th>Port</th><th>License</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Grafana Loki</strong></td><td>Log aggregation &amp; storage backend</td><td><code>3100</code></td><td>AGPL-3.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Promtail</strong></td><td>Log collector agent (file tailing + push)</td><td>—</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Grafana</strong></td><td>Dashboard, search, alerting UI</td><td><code>3200</code></td><td>AGPL-3.0</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- 7. ARCHITECTURE                                                     -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="architecture" class="section">
  <div class="section-title">7. Architecture</div>
  <div class="section-sub">How logs flow from applications to Grafana dashboards.</div>

  <div class="card">
    <pre class="code">┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        APPLICATION LAYER                              │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐ │
│  │ DevTeam Hub │  │ TDI2         │  │ NestJS App │  │ Next.js App │ │
│  │ Rails 8.1   │  │ ASP.NET Core │  │ TypeScript │  │ TypeScript  │ │
│  │ Lograge JSON│  │ Serilog JSON │  │ Pino JSON  │  │ Pino JSON   │ │
│  └──────┬──────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └─────┬──────┘  └──────┬──────┘ │
│         │                │                 │                │        │
│         ▼                ▼                 ▼                ▼        │
│    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐       │
│    │              JSON logs → STDOUT / file                   │       │
│    └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘       │
└───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       COLLECTION LAYER                                │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Promtail Agent                                                 │  │
│  │  • Tails log files / Docker stdout                              │  │
│  │  • Adds labels: {service, env, level, host}                     │  │
│  │  • Pushes to Loki via HTTP POST                                 │  │
│  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                              │                                        │
│  ┌──────────────────────┐   │   ┌─────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ .NET 4.8.1 Apps      │   │   │ Jenkins CI                      │  │
│  │ (Windows EventLog)   │───┘   │ Build logs via Loki plugin      │  │
│  │ Promtail on Windows  │       │ or Promtail on Jenkins host     │  │
│  └──────────────────────┘       └─────────────┬───────────────────┘  │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘
                                                │
                            ┌───────────────────┘
                            ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       STORAGE LAYER                                   │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Grafana Loki (:3100)                                           │  │
│  │  • Receives log streams via HTTP Push API                       │  │
│  │  • Indexes labels only (not content) → low storage              │  │
│  │  • Retention: 30d production, 7d staging, 3d development        │  │
│  │  • LogQL queries for search &amp; filtering                        │  │
│  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       VISUALIZATION LAYER                             │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Grafana (:3200)                                                │  │
│  │  • Log search &amp; exploration (Explore view)                     │  │
│  │  • Pre-built dashboards per service                             │  │
│  │  • Error rate alerts → email / webhook to DevTeam Hub           │  │
│  │  • Live tail streaming                                          │  │
│  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                              │                                        │
│  ┌───────────────────────────▼───────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │  DevTeam Hub API ← Grafana webhook alerts                     │    │
│  │  DevTeam Hub API → Loki LogQL queries (read logs in UI)       │    │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>
  </div>
</div>

