## 6. DevTeam Hub Webhook Integration

Jenkins notifies DevTeam Hub after every build by posting to `/webhooks/jenkins`.

**Payload:**

```json
{
  "token": "<DEVTEAM_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>",
  "ref": "refs/heads/main",
  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "build_url": "http://jenkins.devteam.local:8080/job/devteam-hub/42/"
}
```

DevTeam Hub uses this to:
- Update the linked `CiRun` record''s status.
- Broadcast a Turbo Stream update to all connected browsers showing the live CI status badge.
- Trigger notifications if the build fails.

Store the shared secret in Jenkins credentials as `devteam-webhook-token` and reference it
via `env.DEVTEAM_WEBHOOK_TOKEN` (injected by the JCasC configuration above).

---

## 7. Shared Library

Create a `jenkins-shared-library` repository and register it in
**Manage Jenkins → System → Global Pipeline Libraries** (name: `devteam-shared`).

```groovy
// vars/notifyDevTeam.groovy
def call(String status = null) {
    def s = status ?: (currentBuild.result ?: ''SUCCESS'')
    httpRequest(
        url: env.DEVTEAM_WEBHOOK_URL,
        httpMode: ''POST'',
        contentType: ''APPLICATION_JSON'',
        requestBody: """{
            "token":"${env.DEVTEAM_WEBHOOK_TOKEN}",
            "ref":"${env.GIT_BRANCH}",
            "status":"${s}",
            "build_url":"${env.BUILD_URL}"
        }"""
    )
}
```

Then any Jenkinsfile can be simplified to:

```groovy
@Library(''devteam-shared'') _

pipeline {
    // ...
    post {
        always { notifyDevTeam() }
    }
}
```

